  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-53\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n2123f7805b1b7aa7f6651f96342e7ef188ff763e\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2011-07-14 06:08:05 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-618\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-618\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math.complex.ComplexTest::testAddNaN\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math.complex.Complex\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Complex Add and Subtract handle NaN arguments differently, but javadoc contracts are the same\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nFor both Complex add and subtract, the javadoc states that\n\n{code}\n     * If either this or <code>rhs</code> has a NaN value in either part,\n     * {@link #NaN} is returned; otherwise Inifinite and NaN values are\n     * returned in the parts of the result according to the rules for\n     * {@link java.lang.Double} arithmetic\n{code}\n\nSubtract includes an isNaN test and returns Complex.NaN if either complex argument isNaN; but add omits this test.  The test should be added to the add implementation (actually restored, since this looks like a code merge problem going back to 1.1).\n\nComments:\n\n[Phil Steitz]: Fixed in r1146573",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.math.complex.Complex (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.math.complex.Complex (fixed)\n@@ -150,6 +150,9 @@\n     public Complex add(Complex rhs)\n         throws NullArgumentException {\n         MathUtils.checkNotNull(rhs);\n+        if (isNaN || rhs.isNaN) {\n+            return NaN;\n+        }\n         return createComplex(real + rhs.getReal(),\n             imaginary + rhs.getImaginary());\n     }"
}